    <!-- ===== PRIVACY CONTENT ===== -->
    <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
      <div class="container-narrow" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="3">
        <div class="legal-content" style="line-height: 1.8; color: var(--c-text-soft); font-size: 1.05rem;">
          <p>Praesentia Legal ("Praesentia," "we," "our," or "us") respects your privacy and is committed to protecting
            any information which are related to an identified or identifiable natural person (“Personal Information”)
            that you share with us.</p>

          <p>This Privacy & Cookie Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, store and otherwise process Personal
            Information when you access or use our website located at <a
              href="https://www.praesentialegal.com">www.praesentialegal.com</a>, including all associated webpages,
            content and its subdomains (collectively, the "Site"), communicate with us, or otherwise interact with us
            online.</p>

          <p>This Privacy Policy should be read together with our Website Terms of Use and any other notices that may be
            provided at the time we collect your information.</p>

          <p>By accessing or using the Site, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy Policy.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Scope</h3>
          <p>This Privacy Policy applies to information collected through the Site and through communications initiated
            through the Site, including email communications and contact forms.</p>
          <p>This Privacy Policy does not apply to:</p>
          <ul
            style="padding-left: var(--sp-5); margin-bottom: var(--sp-5); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--sp-2);">
            <li>information collected offline except where specifically incorporated by reference;</li>
            <li>third-party websites or services that may be linked from the Site;</li>
            <li>information processed solely on behalf of clients pursuant to a separate engagement agreement; or</li>
            <li>employment-related information collected in connection with recruitment unless otherwise stated.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Who We Are</h3>
          <p>Praesentia is a legal services company that provides legal, commercial, compliance, privacy, governance and
            related advisory services to businesses.</p>
          <p>Unless otherwise stated, Praesentia is the controller (or equivalent under applicable privacy laws) of the
            Personal Information collected through the Site.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Information We Collect</h3>
          <p>The categories of information we collect depend upon how you interact with the Site.</p>

          <h4 style="color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-5); margin-bottom: var(--sp-3); font-size: 1.2rem;">
            Information You Provide</h4>
          <p>We may collect information that you voluntarily provide, including:</p>
          <ul
            style="padding-left: var(--sp-5); margin-bottom: var(--sp-5); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--sp-2);">
            <li>your name;</li>
            <li>business name;</li>
            <li>employer;</li>
            <li>job title;</li>
            <li>email address;</li>
            <li>telephone number;</li>
            <li>country or region;</li>
            <li>the contents of your communications with us;</li>
            <li>information submitted through contact forms;</li>
            <li>information contained in emails or correspondence;</li>
            <li>information you provide when subscribing to newsletters, updates or events; and</li>
            <li>any other information you voluntarily choose to provide.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>You should only provide information that is relevant to your inquiry.</p>

          <h4 style="color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-5); margin-bottom: var(--sp-3); font-size: 1.2rem;">
            Business Information</h4>
          <p>Where you interact with us on behalf of an organization, we may collect business contact information
            including:</p>
          <ul
            style="padding-left: var(--sp-5); margin-bottom: var(--sp-5); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--sp-2);">
            <li>company name;</li>
            <li>business address;</li>
            <li>department;</li>
            <li>professional role;</li>
            <li>business email address and telephone number; and</li>
            <li>information relating to your organization's inquiry.</li>
          </ul>

          <h4 style="color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-5); margin-bottom: var(--sp-3); font-size: 1.2rem;">
            Information Automatically Collected</h4>
          <p>When you access the Site, certain technical information may be collected automatically. This may include:
          </p>
          <ul
            style="padding-left: var(--sp-5); margin-bottom: var(--sp-5); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--sp-2);">
            <li>IP address;</li>
            <li>browser type and version;</li>
            <li>operating system;</li>
            <li>device type;</li>
            <li>language preferences;</li>
            <li>pages viewed;</li>
            <li>referring website;</li>
            <li>date and time of access;</li>
            <li>session duration;</li>
            <li>clickstream information;</li>
            <li>general geographic location inferred from your IP address; and</li>
            <li>diagnostic and security information.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>This information is generally collected through server logs, cookies and similar technologies.</p>
          <p>We use this information to operate, maintain and secure the Site, diagnose technical issues, monitor
            performance, prevent fraud, abuse and unauthorized access, and improve the functionality and security of the
            Site. We do not use this information for targeted advertising, cross-context behavioural advertising or to
            create profiles about you based on your browsing activities.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Cookies and Similar Technologies</h3>
          <p>We and our hosting or technology providers may use cookies or similar technologies that are necessary for
            the operation, security and performance of the Site. These technologies may be used to maintain the
            functionality of the Site, enhance security, prevent abuse and generate basic technical information about
            website usage.</p>
          <p>We do not currently use cookies or similar technologies for targeted advertising or cross-context
            behavioural advertising.</p>
          <p>If we introduce non-essential cookies, such as analytics or marketing cookies, we will update this Privacy
            Policy and, where required by applicable law, request your consent before such cookies are placed on your
            device.</p>
          <p>Most web browsers allow you to manage or disable cookies through your browser settings. Please note that
            disabling certain cookies may affect the functionality of the Site.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Information from Third Parties</h3>
          <p>We may receive information about you from third parties including:</p>
          <ul
            style="padding-left: var(--sp-5); margin-bottom: var(--sp-5); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--sp-2);">
            <li>publicly available sources;</li>
            <li>professional networking platforms (such as LinkedIn);</li>
            <li>business partners;</li>
            <li>service providers;</li>
            <li>referral sources;</li>
            <li>event organizers; and</li>
            <li>marketing partners, where permitted by applicable law.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We may combine such information with information collected directly from you.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Sensitive Information</h3>
          <p>We do not intentionally request or require sensitive personal information through the Site.</p>
          <p>Please do not submit confidential, privileged, sensitive personal information, health information,
            government-issued identification numbers, financial account information or other highly sensitive
            information through the Site unless specifically requested by us as part of an established client
            engagement.</p>
          <p>If you voluntarily provide such information outside the scope of an engagement, you do so at your own
            discretion.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            How We Use Your Information</h3>
          <p>We may use Personal Information for the following purposes:</p>
          <ul
            style="padding-left: var(--sp-5); margin-bottom: var(--sp-5); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--sp-2);">
            <li>responding to inquiries;</li>
            <li>communicating with you;</li>
            <li>providing requested information;</li>
            <li>evaluating potential client engagements;</li>
            <li>managing our relationship with clients and prospective clients;</li>
            <li>scheduling meetings;</li>
            <li>providing newsletters or legal updates where requested;</li>
            <li>administering events and webinars;</li>
            <li>operating, maintaining and improving the Site;</li>
            <li>monitoring website performance;</li>
            <li>detecting fraud, abuse and unauthorized activity;</li>
            <li>protecting the security of the Site;</li>
            <li>enforcing our legal rights;</li>
            <li>complying with legal obligations;</li>
            <li>maintaining business records;</li>
            <li>carrying out internal administrative functions;</li>
            <li>conducting analytics;</li>
            <li>improving our services; and</li>
            <li>any other purpose disclosed at the time information is collected or otherwise permitted by law.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We may also aggregate or de-identify information so that it no longer identifies an individual. We may use
            such aggregated or de-identified information for any lawful business purpose.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Compliance with Applicable Privacy Laws</h3>
          <p>Praesentia is committed to processing Personal Information in accordance with applicable privacy and data
            protection laws.</p>
          <p>Depending on your location and the nature of your interaction with us, your Personal Information may be
            processed in accordance with applicable laws, including:</p>
          <ul
            style="padding-left: var(--sp-5); margin-bottom: var(--sp-5); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--sp-2);">
            <li>the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (India) ("DPDP Act");</li>
            <li>the General Data Protection Regulation (EU) 2016/679 ("GDPR");</li>
            <li>the UK General Data Protection Regulation and the UK Data Protection Act 2018;</li>
            <li>the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act ("CCPA"); and</li>
            <li>other applicable privacy and data protection laws.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Where a particular privacy law grants you rights or imposes obligations that differ from those described in
            this Privacy Policy, the applicable law will govern to the extent required.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Individuals Located in the EEA, UK and Switzerland</h3>
          <p>Where the GDPR or UK GDPR applies to our processing of your Personal Information, we process your Personal
            Information only where we have a lawful basis to do so, including:</p>
          <ul
            style="padding-left: var(--sp-5); margin-bottom: var(--sp-5); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--sp-2);">
            <li>your consent;</li>
            <li>the performance of a contract or taking steps at your request prior to entering into a contract;</li>
            <li>compliance with legal obligations; or</li>
            <li>our legitimate business interests, provided such interests are not overridden by your rights and
              freedoms.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Where required by applicable law, we implement appropriate safeguards for international transfers of
            Personal Information, including the use of Standard Contractual Clauses or other legally recognized transfer
            mechanisms.</p>
          <p>You also have the rights described in the "Your Privacy Rights" section of this Privacy Policy, including
            the rights to access, rectify, erase, restrict or object to processing, request data portability, withdraw
            consent where applicable, and lodge a complaint with the competent supervisory authority.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Individuals Located in India</h3>
          <p>Where the DPDP Act applies, Praesentia processes Digital Personal Data only for lawful purposes and in
            accordance with applicable legal requirements.</p>
          <p>Subject to the DPDP Act, you may have the right to:</p>
          <ul
            style="padding-left: var(--sp-5); margin-bottom: var(--sp-5); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--sp-2);">
            <li>obtain information regarding the processing of your Digital Personal Data;</li>
            <li>request correction, completion or updating of inaccurate or incomplete Personal Information;</li>
            <li>request the erasure of your Personal Information, subject to applicable legal requirements;</li>
            <li>withdraw consent where processing is based on consent;</li>
            <li>nominate another individual to exercise your rights in accordance with applicable law; and</li>
            <li>seek redress of grievances relating to the processing of your Personal Information.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Requests relating to your Personal Information may be submitted using the contact details provided at the
            end of this Privacy Policy.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Disclosure of Personal Information</h3>
          <p>We do not sell your Personal Information.</p>
          <p>We may disclose your Personal Information only as described in this Privacy Policy or as otherwise
            permitted or required by applicable law.</p>
          <p>We may share your Personal Information with:</p>

          <h5 style="color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-4); margin-bottom: var(--sp-2); font-size: 1.1rem;">
            Service Providers</h5>
          <p>Third-party vendors, consultants and service providers that assist us in operating our business and the
            Site, including providers of website hosting, cloud storage, IT support, cybersecurity, communications,
            analytics, customer relationship management, marketing, and other business support services. Such providers
            are permitted to process Personal Information only on our instructions and only for the purposes for which
            they have been engaged.</p>

          <h5 style="color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-4); margin-bottom: var(--sp-2); font-size: 1.1rem;">
            Professional Advisers</h5>
          <p>Our legal counsel, accountants, auditors, insurers, financial advisers and other professional advisers
            where disclosure is reasonably necessary for the provision of professional services or to protect our legal
            interests.</p>

          <h5 style="color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-4); margin-bottom: var(--sp-2); font-size: 1.1rem;">
            Business Transfers</h5>
          <p>In connection with an actual or proposed merger, acquisition, investment, financing, corporate
            restructuring, sale of assets or other business transaction, provided appropriate safeguards are
            implemented.</p>

          <h5 style="color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-4); margin-bottom: var(--sp-2); font-size: 1.1rem;">
            Legal Compliance</h5>
          <p>Where disclosure is necessary to comply with applicable law, court orders or legal process; respond to
            lawful requests from governmental or regulatory authorities; establish, exercise or defend legal claims;
            enforce our agreements; protect the rights, property or safety of Praesentia, our clients or others; or
            investigate fraud, security incidents or suspected unlawful activity.</p>

          <h5 style="color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-4); margin-bottom: var(--sp-2); font-size: 1.1rem;">With
            Your Consent</h5>
          <p>We may disclose your Personal Information to other parties where you have requested or expressly authorized
            such disclosure.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            International Transfers</h3>
          <p>Praesentia is based in India and may process or store Personal Information in India or in other
            jurisdictions where our service providers, business partners or affiliates operate.</p>
          <p>Accordingly, your Personal Information may be transferred to countries whose data protection laws differ
            from those of your country of residence.</p>
          <p>Where required by applicable law, we implement appropriate safeguards for such transfers, including
            contractual safeguards, organizational measures and reasonable security controls designed to protect
            Personal Information.</p>
          <p>By using the Site or providing your Personal Information, you acknowledge that your information may be
            transferred and processed in accordance with this Privacy Policy.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Data Retention</h3>
          <p>We retain Personal Information only for as long as reasonably necessary to fulfill the purposes described
            in this Privacy Policy, including providing requested services, responding to inquiries, maintaining
            business records, complying with legal or regulatory obligations, resolving disputes, and enforcing our
            agreements.</p>
          <p>When Personal Information is no longer required, we will securely delete, anonymize or otherwise dispose of
            it in accordance with our data retention practices and applicable law.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Data Security</h3>
          <p>We maintain reasonable administrative, technical and physical safeguards designed to protect Personal
            Information against unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration, loss or destruction.</p>
          <p>While we take reasonable steps to safeguard Personal Information, no method of transmission over the
            Internet or electronic storage is completely secure. Accordingly, we cannot guarantee the absolute security
            of any information transmitted to or through the Site.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Marketing Communications</h3>
          <p>Where permitted by applicable law, we may send you newsletters, legal updates, event invitations,
            publications or other communications relating to our services. You may opt out of receiving marketing
            communications at any time by using the unsubscribe mechanism included in our communications or by
            contacting us.</p>
          <p>Even if you opt out of marketing communications, we may continue to send you communications relating to
            existing engagements, legal obligations, security matters or other administrative purposes.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Your Choices</h3>
          <p>Subject to applicable law, you may choose to decline to provide certain Personal Information, unsubscribe
            from marketing communications, manage cookies through browser settings, or request updates to inaccurate
            information.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Third-Party Websites and Services</h3>
          <p>The Site may contain links to third-party websites, applications or services that are not owned or
            controlled by Praesentia. We are not responsible for the privacy practices of third-party websites and
            recommend reviewing their respective privacy policies.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Confidential Information</h3>
          <p>The Site is intended to facilitate general communications with Praesentia. Unless and until we have agreed
            to provide services under a formal engagement, information submitted through the Site or by email should not
            include confidential or sensitive information. Submission of information does not create a client
            relationship.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Your Privacy Rights</h3>
          <p>Depending on your jurisdiction and applicable law, you may have certain rights regarding your Personal
            Information, including rights of access, correction, deletion, restriction, objection, portability, and
            consent withdrawal. To exercise any applicable rights, please contact us.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Additional Information for EEA, UK and Swiss Residents</h3>
          <p>Where the GDPR, UK GDPR or Swiss laws apply, you have the right to lodge a complaint with your competent
            supervisory authority. We do not use automated decision-making or profiling that produces legal or similarly
            significant effects.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Additional Information for California Residents</h3>
          <p>If you are a California resident, you have the right to know what Personal Information we collect, request
            deletion, correct inaccuracies, and not be discriminated against under the CCPA. We do not sell or share
            Personal Information as defined under the CCPA.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Children's Privacy</h3>
          <p>The Site is not directed to children, and we do not knowingly collect Personal Information from individuals
            under 18. If we become aware that we have inadvertently collected information from a child, we will take
            steps to delete it.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
            Changes to this Privacy Policy</h3>
          <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we make material changes, we will update the
            "Effective Date" at the beginning of the policy. Your continued use of the Site constitutes your
            acknowledgment of the revised policy.</p>

          <h3
            style="font-family: var(--ff-serif); color: var(--c-text); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); font-size: 1.5rem;">
